Follow-up to k252. The text form of `ocp status` shows the AMD GPU nodes (allocatable/capacity, gfx targets, effective allocation and its source), the ResourceSlices of driver gpu.amd.com, and the AMD DaemonSets. `--json` (a machine interface, see k230) does not carry them yet.

Shape (main agent's call): extend the existing GPU part of the JSON object in the style of the NVIDIA keys. Per AMD node: name, allocatable, capacity, gfx_targets (list), allocation, allocation_source (node-label|config). Then resource_slices per node (device count), and daemonsets keyed like %OCP::Drift::AMD_GPU_DAEMONSETS with namespace, name, ready, desired and state (ready|partial|not-deployed|unknown). Keep it canonical with sorted keys. Clusters without AMD nodes must produce byte-identical output.

Also consolidate the constants: `amd.com/gpu` and `gpu.amd.com` are local to Status.pm. If k251 also needs them, move them to OCP::Config next to $AMD_GPU_PRESENT_LABEL (state lane), so there is no second copy. Lane: ocp-status-worker (+ state for the constants).

2026-10-31 02:12 Shape decision (ocp-status-worker; card asked to say why if nesting differs): the JSON has no GPU object to extend. The only GPU key is nodes[].gpu, the per-node nvidia.com/gpu capacity. The AMD part has cluster-level pieces (slices, DaemonSets) that cannot live in a node entry, and the card's per-node entries carry their own name. So it is one top-level 'amd_gpu' object { nodes[], resource_slices, daemonsets }, present only when the cluster has an AMD node (same test as the text form). nodes[].gpu stays the NVIDIA count. Choices made here, not by the maintainer: allocatable defaults to 0 and capacity to null when absent (the text form treats them the same way). gfx_targets is the sorted, unique target names; per-target counts are not carried (the text form shows them). resource_slices is {state: served|not-served|unknown, devices: {node: n}}; the state wrapper exists because the card's rule wants state 'unknown' on a read error. devices is {} when not served and null when unknown. DaemonSet state 'ready' includes 0 of 0. ready and desired are null unless the DaemonSet was read.
Constants: lib/OCP/Config.pm is unchanged (git diff empty), so I kept the local copies in Status.pm and did not touch Config. k251's lib/OCP/Cmd/Apply/AMDGPU.pm now holds a second local copy (amd.com/gpu, gpu.amd.com, plus amd.com/), and its comment says 'k258 moves both onto shared variables in OCP::Config'. k258 did not do that, so the consolidation is still open, for the state lane.

